        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your dryer plug and your wall outlet do not match, swap the cord. A 4-wire cord like the Whirlpool PT400L for a 14-30R outlet, or a 3-wire PT220L for an existing 10-30R, costs $20 to $35, takes 20 minutes, and gives you the connection the dryer was designed for, with the bonding strap set correctly and no extra plug joint behind the machine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy an adapter only as a short bridge, choose a 30-amp, 10 AWG, genuinely listed one, and check it after the first loads. If the outlet is damaged, the circuit has no ground and must change, or the breaker trips, stop shopping for plugs and call an electrician. That is the fix that actually ends the problem.
          </p>
